    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const item = $('code 1').item.json;\nconst recentTrades = $input.all(); // rows from Get many rows1\nconst sameSymbolCount = recentTrades.length;\n\nconst { reasoning, confidence, ...rest } = item;\nconst verifierInput = { ...rest, recent_trades_on_symbol: sameSymbolCount };\n\nconst prompt = `You are a risk verifier for an options trading signal. You do NOT have access to the proposer's stated reasoning or confidence score — evaluate this trade independently based only on the trade parameters below:\n${JSON.stringify(verifierInput)}\nIf ANY rule_result is \"failed\", set approved to false regardless of other factors — a failed risk rule is an automatic veto, not one factor among several.\n\nCheck the following, using only the trade parameters given (no reasoning text is available to you):\n1. Is the symbol a well-formed, plausible options contract identifier (correct format: underlying, expiry, strike, call/put)?\n2. Is the side/qty reasonable on its own terms (e.g. qty <= 1 for a single-position test strategy)?\n3. Does the action type (TRADE/HOLD) and order_type make sense as a valid, executable instruction?\n4. Would this trade fit prudent risk management for a single-position size (qty 1, not oversized)?\nIf action is \"HOLD\", confirm holding is a safe default and set approved to true.\nAlso evaluate these specific risk rules and report pass/fail for each, based only on the trade parameters:\n- position_limit: does qty stay within a safe single-position size (qty <= 1)?\n- daily_loss_limit: does the order type/side avoid unbounded exposure (e.g. market order vs. unlimited size)?\n- concentration_limit: does recent_trades_on_symbol exceed 2 in the lookback window? If so, fail; otherwise pass.\nRespond ONLY in valid JSON, no extra text, in this exact shape:\n{\"approved\": true or false, \"confidence\": 0-100, \"reason\": \"short explanation\", \"rule_results\": {\"position_limit\": \"passed\" or \"failed\", \"daily_loss_limit\": \"passed\" or \"failed\", \"concentration_limit\": \"passed\" or \"failed\"}}`;\n\nconst requestBody = {\n  contents: [\n    {\n      parts: [\n        { text: prompt }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n};\nreturn [{ json: { requestBody } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1280,
